stmd:study-38484744 a stm:Study ; stm:pmid "38484744" ; dcterms:title "Can large language models replace humans in the systematic review process? Evaluating GPT-4's efficacy in screening and extracting data from peer-reviewed and grey literature in multiple languages" ; dcterms:date "2024" ; stm:selectionRoute "report_referenced" ; stm:doi "10.1002/jrsm.1715" .
stmd:record-38484744 a stm:EvaluationRecord ; stm:aboutStudy stmd:study-38484744 ; stm:extractedOn "2026-09-11"^^xsd:date ; stm:extractedBy "evidence-extractor-agent" ;
  stm:hasEvidence stmd:evidence-38484744-E01, stmd:evidence-38484744-E02, stmd:evidence-38484744-E03, stmd:evidence-38484744-E04, stmd:evidence-38484744-E05, stmd:evidence-38484744-E06, stmd:evidence-38484744-E07, stmd:evidence-38484744-E08a, stmd:evidence-38484744-E08b, stmd:evidence-38484744-E08c, stmd:evidence-38484744-E09, stmd:evidence-38484744-E10, stmd:evidence-38484744-E11, stmd:evidence-38484744-E12, stmd:evidence-38484744-E13, stmd:evidence-38484744-E14, stmd:evidence-38484744-E15, stmd:evidence-38484744-E16, stmd:evidence-38484744-E17, stmd:evidence-38484744-E18, stmd:evidence-38484744-E19, stmd:evidence-38484744-E20, stmd:evidence-38484744-E21, stmd:evidence-38484744-E22, stmd:evidence-38484744-E23, stmd:evidence-38484744-E24, stmd:evidence-38484744-E25, stmd:evidence-38484744-E26, stmd:evidence-38484744-E27, stmd:evidence-38484744-E28, stmd:evidence-38484744-E29, stmd:evidence-38484744-E30, stmd:evidence-38484744-E31, stmd:evidence-38484744-E32, stmd:evidence-38484744-E33, stmd:evidence-38484744-E34, stmd:evidence-38484744-E35 .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E01 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E01 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Methods, Analysis metrics" ; stm:quote "For GPT-4 performance, we calculated sensitivity, specificity and accuracy, which are commonly used metrics" .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E02 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E02 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Repository: registered protocol description at https://osf.io/bc3gj/ (registration https://osf.io/9e6ym )" ; stm:quote "We will then assess 300 titles and abstracts that are double-reviewed. Of these, we will review 100 titles and abstracts in English language black literature and another 100 titles and abstracts in English language grey literature." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E03 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E03 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Results" ; stm:quote "Peer-reviewed studies in English were fully balanced, as intended by our design, except in the extraction stage (.03; that is, 1 included for every 30 excluded)." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E04 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E04 ; stm:status "absent" ; stm:location "not found" .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E05 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E05 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Abstract" ; stm:quote "This pre-registered study evaluates GPT-4’s capability in title/abstract screening, full-text review, and data extraction across various literature types and languages using a ‘human-out-of-the-loop’ approach." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E06 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E06 ; stm:status "absent" ; stm:location "not found" .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E07 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E07 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Introduction" ; stm:quote "No study, for instance, has tested grey literature and non-English literature, which can constitute a large proportion of the evidence base for some topics (Lawrence et al., 2014)." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E08a a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E08a ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Introduction" ; stm:quote "It is also the first to test an LLM model in reviewing grey literature and literature in other languages." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E08b a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E08b ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Results" ; stm:quote "The balanced dataset of English peer-reviewed literature had lower accuracy (title/abstract: .67, full-text: .69) than the more unbalanced non-English literature dataset (title/abstract: .88, full-text: .96)." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E08c a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E08c ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Results" ; stm:quote "This was especially true in literature containing non-English studies (>.90)." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E09 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E09 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Methods, Analysis metrics" ; stm:quote "Previous studies have reported that human error rates in systematic review screening range from 5% to 20%, implying that a score of 100% is ‘superior’ to humans, while an accuracy score of 80% to 95% for GPT-4 could be regarded as ‘on par’ (Wang et al., 2020)." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E10 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E10 ; stm:status "absent" ; stm:location "not found" .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E11 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E11 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Methods, Prompt engineering approach" ; stm:quote "This approach seemed to reduce hallucinations, a frequently observed phenomenon where an LLM confidently produces an inaccurate output (Beutel et al., 2023), but reduced consistency upon retesting." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E12 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E12 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Discussion" ; stm:quote "Such a limitation will not be easily detected by anecdotal tests (Mahuli et al., 2023; Qureshi et al., 2023) and may mislead general users who may assume that GPT is performing well when it is not." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E13 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E13 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Abstract and Conclusion" ; stm:quote "Our findings indicate that, currently, substantial caution should be used if LLMs are being used to conduct systematic reviews, but suggest that, for certain systematic review tasks delivered under reliable prompts, LLMs can rival human performance." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E14 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E14 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Methods" ; stm:quote "Links to our GPT-4 prompts and outputs, as well as the R code used for analysis, are on the Open Science Foundation (OSF) page (link)." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E15 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E15 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Introduction" ; stm:quote "This model has been reported to significantly surpass all other LLMs, including previous versions of GPT, in various natural language processing tasks across both English and other languages (OpenAI, 2023)." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E16 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E16 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Methods" ; stm:quote "Sample size was largely based on studies reviewed by at least two humans for screening, which was the case for English language documents at all stages and those written in other languages in the title/abstract stage." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E17 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E17 ; stm:status "absent" ; stm:location "not found" .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E18 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E18 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Repository: https://osf.io/bc3gj/ , Data and code, Raw data title abstract.xlsx" ; stm:quote "https://chat.openai.com/share/dc94cb4e-82ce-4ea5-aa36-3d3e4011e1e5" .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E19 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E19 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Methods, Screening and extraction" ; stm:quote "We proceeded to the next criterion in another chat if GPT-4 responded ‘yes/maybe’. A ‘no’ meant exclusion from further review." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E20 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E20 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Methods" ; stm:quote "We tested documents that were reviewed using four inclusion/exclusion criteria: containing empirical data, parenting behaviour, refugee status, and protracted refugee situation." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E21 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E21 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Methods, Analysis metrics" ; stm:quote "We also used weighted kappa to better capture the severity of false rejections by GPT-4, which are the most serious errors it can make, because this would exclude a study which meets the inclusion criteria." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E22 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E22 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Introduction" ; stm:quote "A few may have included contaminated data, such as Guo et al., (2023) and Syriani et al., (2023), who used datasets for systematic reviews that published their results before or in 2021, when GPT was trained, which may bias the results in favour of GPT." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E23 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E23 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Methods, Prompt engineering approach" ; stm:quote "Presenting criteria and text within the same message and lowering the number of studies based on the criterion’s complexity improved consistency without increasing hallucinations." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E24 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E24 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Methods, Prompt engineering approach" ; stm:quote "We assessed test-retest reliability using 10 studies on each of our four criteria. Each criterion corresponds to a prompt. We tested the four prompts five times and generated five decisions per criterion per study." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E25 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E25 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Methods" ; stm:quote "We registered this study protocol on the OSF, while the details of the review can be found on both OSF (link) and PROSPERO (Anonymised)." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E26 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E26 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "References, and Introduction" ; stm:quote "OpenAI (2023). Gpt-4 technical report. arXiv:2303.08774." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E27 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E27 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Methods" ; stm:quote "We used the ChatGPT interface to access the GPT-4 model between May and September 2023." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E28 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E28 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Methods" ; stm:quote "While we ensured a mix of decisions in terms of a random selection of relevant and irrelevant studies written in English to gain deeper insight into inclusion performance, this was generally not possible for non-English studies due to the large number of excluded studies." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E29 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E29 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Discussion" ; stm:quote "We also observe that the ‘parenting behaviour’ prompt might have been most challenging for GPT-4 because the prompt was more open than specific (to capture non-traditional ways of parenting), unlike all other ones, which contained exact definitions." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E30 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E30 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Methods, Screening and extraction" ; stm:quote "Each abstract batch (a maximum of three abstracts for the protracted concept – given that it contained a longer prompt – and five abstracts for other concepts) underwent four chat tests based on inclusion/exclusion criteria." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E31 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E31 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Discussion" ; stm:quote "There are three main strengths and weaknesses to this study. First, despite our comprehensive approach covering various literature types and our efforts to achieve balance, the challenges in balancing non-English texts and our very attempts at balancing could have both introduced biases." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E32 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E32 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Results" ; stm:quote "Supporting this notion, the associated adjusted kappa scores were low, ranging from ‘none’ to ‘moderate’ as categorised by McHugh (2012)." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E33 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E33 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Discussion" ; stm:quote "Third, we registered and documented our research protocol and analysis plan to ensure its validity and replicability but might have benefited from also creating a detailed plan for prompt engineering in advance." .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E34 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E34 ; stm:status "absent" ; stm:location "not found" .
stmd:evidence-38484744-E35 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E35 ; stm:status "absent" ; stm:location "not found" .

stmd:study-39151163 a stm:Study ; stm:pmid "39151163" ; dcterms:title "Human-Comparable Sensitivity of Large Language Models in Identifying Eligible Studies Through Title and Abstract Screening: 3-Layer Strategy Using GPT-3.5 and GPT-4 for Systematic Reviews" ; dcterms:date "2024" ; stm:selectionRoute "sampled" ; stm:pmcid "PMC11364944" ; stm:doi "10.2196/52758" .
stmd:record-39151163 a stm:EvaluationRecord ; stm:aboutStudy stmd:study-39151163 ; stm:extractedOn "2026-09-11"^^xsd:date ; stm:extractedBy "claude-opus-5-evidence-extractor" ;
  stm:hasEvidence stmd:evidence-39151163-E01, stmd:evidence-39151163-E02, stmd:evidence-39151163-E03, stmd:evidence-39151163-E04, stmd:evidence-39151163-E05, stmd:evidence-39151163-E06, stmd:evidence-39151163-E07, stmd:evidence-39151163-E08a, stmd:evidence-39151163-E08b, stmd:evidence-39151163-E08c, stmd:evidence-39151163-E09, stmd:evidence-39151163-E10, stmd:evidence-39151163-E11, stmd:evidence-39151163-E12, stmd:evidence-39151163-E13, stmd:evidence-39151163-E14, stmd:evidence-39151163-E15, stmd:evidence-39151163-E16, stmd:evidence-39151163-E17, stmd:evidence-39151163-E18, stmd:evidence-39151163-E19, stmd:evidence-39151163-E20, stmd:evidence-39151163-E21, stmd:evidence-39151163-E22, stmd:evidence-39151163-E23, stmd:evidence-39151163-E24, stmd:evidence-39151163-E25, stmd:evidence-39151163-E26, stmd:evidence-39151163-E27, stmd:evidence-39151163-E28, stmd:evidence-39151163-E29, stmd:evidence-39151163-E30, stmd:evidence-39151163-E31, stmd:evidence-39151163-E32, stmd:evidence-39151163-E33, stmd:evidence-39151163-E34, stmd:evidence-39151163-E35 .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E01 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E01 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Methods, Data Analysis" ; stm:quote "We assessed the inclusion or exclusion decisions made by each human evaluator (before consensus was reached) against those determined by GPT-3.5 or GPT-4, focusing on sensitivity and specificity" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E02 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E02 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Abstract, Methods; and Methods, Process of Screening and Prompt Engineering, Table 1" ; stm:quote "We conducted screenings on 2 of our previous systematic reviews related to the treatment of bipolar disorder, with 1381 records from the first review and 3146 from the second" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E03 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E03 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Methods, Process of Screening and Prompt Engineering" ; stm:quote "Of these, 30 records were targeted for a full-text assessment, and eventually 6 records (encompassing 6 studies) were selected for meta-analysis" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E04 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E04 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Results, Time and Cost Required for Screenings" ; stm:quote "The screening for these 2 studies incurred a total cost of US $59, with US $4 for calls to GPT-3.5 and US $55 for calls to GPT-4" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E05 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E05 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Abstract, Conclusions" ; stm:quote "Our 3-layer screening method with GPT-4 demonstrated acceptable level of sensitivity and specificity that supports its practical application in systematic review screenings" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E06 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E06 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Methods, Data Analysis" ; stm:quote "For records eligible for full-text assessment but excluded by either GPT-3.5 or GPT-4, we reviewed the title and the abstract to assess whether the exclusion decision was justified" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E07 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E07 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Results, Results of the Paper by Maruki et al" ; stm:quote "although the records involved bipolar disorder, they did not match the selection criteria due to the presence of comorbidities (one record had generalized anxiety disorder, and the other had alcohol dependence)" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E08a a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E08a ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Results, Comparison of GPT-3.5, GPT-4, and Human Evaluators" ; stm:quote "The sensitivity and specificity of human evaluators and GPT-3.5 and GPT-4 for each segment are shown in Table 4" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E08b a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E08b ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Results, Results on Takeshima et al Paper; Table 4" ; stm:quote "In the first study, the sensitivities/specificities of the GPT-3.5 and GPT-4 were 0.900/0.709 and 0.806/0.996, respectively" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E08c a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E08c ; stm:status "absent" ; stm:location "not found" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E09 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E09 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Introduction" ; stm:quote "For systematic reviews, maintaining high sensitivity for studies eligible for full-text assessment, ideally at 100% [ 10 ], is crucial if they are to be fully supplanted by an automated process" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E10 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E10 ; stm:status "absent" ; stm:location "not found" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E11 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E11 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Abstract, Results; and Discussion, Principal Findings" ; stm:quote "Further investigation indicated that the cases incorrectly excluded by GPT-3.5 were due to a lack of domain knowledge, while the cases incorrectly excluded by GPT-4 were due to misinterpretations of the inclusion criteria" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E12 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E12 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Discussion, Principal Findings" ; stm:quote "A potential future risk is that the normalization of AI-based judgments could result in the oversight of human expert verification, potentially diminishing the quality of systematic reviews" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E13 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E13 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Abstract, Conclusions; and Limitations" ; stm:quote "Future research should aim to generalize this approach and explore its effectiveness in diverse settings, both medical and nonmedical, to fully establish its use and operational feasibility" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E14 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E14 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Methods, Calling the GPT-3.5 and GPT-4 API" ; stm:quote "The Apps Script used in this study is shown in Multimedia Appendix 1" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E15 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E15 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Introduction" ; stm:quote "GPT-3.5 has shown exceptional performance in the medical domain, achieving remarkable results on medical licensing examinations across different regions [ 4 ]. Furthermore, GPT-4, the successor to GPT-3.5, has exhibited superior performance" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E16 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E16 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Introduction; and Methods, Process of Screening and Prompt Engineering" ; stm:quote "In this study, we regarded the results of human screening as the gold standard and calculated the sensitivity and specificity of the GPT-3.5 and GPT-4 screening results in comparison with them" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E17 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E17 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Methods, Calling the GPT-3.5 and GPT-4 API" ; stm:quote "In light of these observations, and primarily to ensure reproducibility, this study fixed the temperature at 0 for all screenings" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E18 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E18 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Textbox 2, structure of the prompts used for each of the 3 layers" ; stm:quote "You are a researcher rigorously screening titles and abstracts of scientific papers for inclusion or exclusion in a review paper. Does the paper with the above title and abstract meet the specified research design? If yes, highly suspected, or difficult to determine, answer 'I'. If not, answer 'E'." .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E19 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E19 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Methods, Process of Screening and Prompt Engineering" ; stm:quote "Within these prompts, we specified that if a decision cannot be made, records should be considered potentially eligible for full-text assessment and not excluded" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E20 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E20 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Methods, Process of Screening and Prompt Engineering" ; stm:quote "In this study, we extracted information by inserting the text from the “inclusion criteria” paragraph of the Methods section of each paper into the specified location in the prompt" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E21 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E21 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Abstract, Objective" ; stm:quote "Our goal is to develop a screening method that maximizes sensitivity for identifying relevant records" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E22 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E22 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Limitations" ; stm:quote "gpt-3.5-turbo-0125’s training data include information up to September 2021, whereas gpt-4-0125-preview’s training data extend to December 2023 [ 35 ]. Consequently, the systematic review paper by Takeshima et al [ 38 ] might have been incorporated into GPT-3.5’s training data set" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E23 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E23 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Discussion, Principal Findings" ; stm:quote "One primary concern is their susceptibility to misinformation and quality issues inherent in their training data" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E24 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E24 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Limitations" ; stm:quote "However, our observations indicate no variation in results across multiple tests with the same model in this study" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E25 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E25 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Methods, Process of Screening and Prompt Engineering, Table 1" ; stm:quote "Databases Ovid MEDLINE, Cochrane Central Register of Controlled Trials, Embase, PsycINFO, and ClinicalTrials.gov PubMed, Cochrane Central Register of Controlled Trials, and Embase Number of records screened 1381 3146" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E26 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E26 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Discussion, Principal Findings; and References 35 and 36" ; stm:quote "Furthermore, the decision-making processes of LLMs lack transparency, making them difficult to interpret" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E27 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E27 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Methods, Language Model Details" ; stm:quote "For gpt-3.5-turbo, we used the most current model available, gpt-3.5-turbo-0125" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E28 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E28 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Abstract, Methods; and Methods, Process of Screening and Prompt Engineering" ; stm:quote "We conducted screenings on 2 of our previous systematic reviews related to the treatment of bipolar disorder, with 1381 records from the first review and 3146 from the second" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E29 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E29 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Methods, Data Analysis; Results; Multimedia Appendix 2" ; stm:quote "Furthermore, for records that were incorrectly excluded by GPT-3.5 or GPT-4, we conducted a narrative verification of the erroneous judgments by asking each LLM to explain the reasons behind their decisions" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E30 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E30 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Methods, Calling the GPT-3.5 and GPT-4 API" ; stm:quote "In this study, we used Google Spreadsheet and Google Apps Script to interface with the GPT-3.5 and GPT-4 APIs for batch processing" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E31 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E31 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Limitations" ; stm:quote "This study has some limitations. First, the 2 systematic reviews used in this investigation [ 38 , 39 ] were confined to clinical studies within psychiatry, limiting the generalizability of our findings" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E32 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E32 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Results, Results on Takeshima et al Paper and Results of the Paper by Maruki et al" ; stm:quote "For the one record that GPT-3.5 determined to be excluded at the target population layer, it was suggested that GPT-3.5 concluded that the record “included both bipolar disorder and unipolar mood disorder, which did not match the selection criteria" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E33 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E33 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Discussion, Principal Findings" ; stm:quote "Although achieving 100% sensitivity remained unattainable, a 3-layer screening method with GPT-4 may potentially be practical for use in the systematic review process and can reduce human labor" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E34 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E34 ; stm:status "absent" ; stm:location "not found" .
stmd:evidence-39151163-E35 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E35 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Results, Time and Cost Required for Screenings" ; stm:quote "The screening for these 2 studies incurred a total cost of US $59, with US $4 for calls to GPT-3.5 and US $55 for calls to GPT-4" .

stmd:study-40119675 a stm:Study ; stm:pmid "40119675" ; dcterms:title "High-performance automated abstract screening with large language model ensembles" ; dcterms:date "2025" ; stm:selectionRoute "sampled" ; stm:pmcid "PMC12012331" ; stm:doi "10.1093/jamia/ocaf050" .
stmd:record-40119675 a stm:EvaluationRecord ; stm:aboutStudy stmd:study-40119675 ; stm:extractedOn "2026-09-11"^^xsd:date ; stm:extractedBy "claude-opus-5-evidence-extractor" ;
  stm:hasEvidence stmd:evidence-40119675-E01, stmd:evidence-40119675-E02, stmd:evidence-40119675-E03, stmd:evidence-40119675-E04, stmd:evidence-40119675-E05, stmd:evidence-40119675-E06, stmd:evidence-40119675-E07, stmd:evidence-40119675-E08a, stmd:evidence-40119675-E08b, stmd:evidence-40119675-E08c, stmd:evidence-40119675-E09, stmd:evidence-40119675-E10, stmd:evidence-40119675-E11, stmd:evidence-40119675-E12, stmd:evidence-40119675-E13, stmd:evidence-40119675-E14, stmd:evidence-40119675-E15, stmd:evidence-40119675-E16, stmd:evidence-40119675-E17, stmd:evidence-40119675-E18, stmd:evidence-40119675-E19, stmd:evidence-40119675-E20, stmd:evidence-40119675-E21, stmd:evidence-40119675-E22, stmd:evidence-40119675-E23, stmd:evidence-40119675-E24, stmd:evidence-40119675-E25, stmd:evidence-40119675-E26, stmd:evidence-40119675-E27, stmd:evidence-40119675-E28, stmd:evidence-40119675-E29, stmd:evidence-40119675-E30, stmd:evidence-40119675-E31, stmd:evidence-40119675-E32, stmd:evidence-40119675-E33, stmd:evidence-40119675-E34, stmd:evidence-40119675-E35 .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E01 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E01 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Materials and methods, Performance metrics" ; stm:quote "Sensitivity, specificity, and accuracy calculations were subsequently performed to provide interpretable measures of abstract screening performance" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E02 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E02 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Materials and methods, Data selection and preparation" ; stm:quote "The initial corpus comprised 128 299 articles from replicated and de-duplicated searches across all 23 systematic reviews. During data cleaning, 8604 articles (6.71%) with missing abstracts were excluded from further analysis, resulting in a final dataset of 119 695 articles" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E03 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E03 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Results, Table 1" ; stm:quote "Lead author Title n (search results) n (included records) Bellon Perioperative glycaemic control for people with diabetes undergoing surgery 3693 23" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E04 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E04 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Materials and methods, Implementation simulation" ; stm:quote "Workload reduction was calculated as the number of correctly excluded articles per 100 screened records; this corresponds to the proportion of articles that human reviewers would not need to appraise subsequently" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E05 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E05 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Discussion" ; stm:quote "Automated systems may instead be used in place of a second reviewer in parallel with human researchers" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E06 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E06 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Materials and methods, Implementation simulation" ; stm:quote "For in parallel ensembles, a single “include” decision from either component was sufficient for article inclusion, whereas for in series ensembles both components had to reach an “include” decision for the article to be included" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E07 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E07 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Discussion, limitations" ; stm:quote "Inter-review variation shows that automated screening may be better suited to some subjects than others, and applications should be specifically validated within a subject or topic if used" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E08a a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E08a ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Materials and methods, Performance metrics" ; stm:quote "Correlation analysis between human and LLM performance was undertaken to explore whether specific reviews were consistently more challenging across both human and LLM screeners" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E08b a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E08b ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Results, LLM can match or exceed human screening performance on a balanced dataset" ; stm:quote "Similar comparative performance was observed when results were stratified by review ( Supplementary Material S2 )" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E08c a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E08c ; stm:status "absent" ; stm:location "not found" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E09 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E09 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Results, Ensemble configurations exhibit useful abstract screening performance" ; stm:quote "Four parallel ensembles exhibited 100% sensitivity, a prerequisite for autonomous deployment" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E10 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E10 ; stm:status "absent" ; stm:location "not found" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E11 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E11 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Materials and methods, LLM pipelines and prompt development" ; stm:quote "false negatives (exclusion of eligible records) are a more damaging error than false positives (including ineligible records for full text screening); because eligible records that are excluded will not be used in subsequent evidence synthesis" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E12 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E12 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Abstract, Discussion" ; stm:quote "LLM-human ensembles can achieve similar benefits while maintaining human oversight over all records" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E13 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E13 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Conclusion" ; stm:quote "LLM performance is subject-specific but can be optimized through prompt engineering, and researchers are advised to conduct domain-specific validation before unsupervised deployment" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E14 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E14 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Materials and methods, Technical details" ; stm:quote "All code required to replicate experiments and analysis is hosted on GitHub ( https://github.com/RohanSanghera/GEN-SYS" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E15 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E15 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Results, Prompt design determines LLM screening behavior" ; stm:quote "GPT-4 was excluded from full dataset evaluation as its successor, GPT-4o, demonstrated superior performance, efficiency, and cost" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E16 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E16 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Materials and methods, Data selection and preparation" ; stm:quote "The inclusion lists of each review were used as the ground truth: gold standard examples of articles which should have been included on the basis of the reviews’ protocols" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E17 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E17 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Materials and methods, Prompt development" ; stm:quote "model parameters were adjusted to produce deterministic, concise outputs suitable for abstract screening: “temperature” and “max_tokens” parameters were specified as 0.2 and 5, respectively" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E18 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E18 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Materials and methods, Prompt development" ; stm:quote "The final wording of each prompt is provided in Supplementary Material S1" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E19 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E19 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Supplement: Supplementary Material 1.rtf, Bias Level: Heavy, fetched from https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12012331/supplementaryFiles" ; stm:quote "If there is any uncertainty if an article fulfils the inclusion criteria, but the abstract appears relevant to the title of the systematic review, lean towards including the article, as long as no exclusion criteria are met." .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E20 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E20 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Materials and methods, Prompt development" ; stm:quote "For each systematic review, prompts were constructed using the task description described above, review’s title, and inclusion criteria" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E21 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E21 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Materials and methods, Prompt development" ; stm:quote "Where models repeatedly returned an error message, content violation note, or no interpretable output, a label of “include” was assigned to avoid excluding potentially eligible records before full text screening" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E22 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E22 ; stm:status "absent" ; stm:location "not found" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E23 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E23 ; stm:status "absent" ; stm:location "not found" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E24 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E24 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Materials and methods, Evaluation methodology" ; stm:quote "In these trials, each LLM-prompt combination was applied 3 times over the development dataset to establish consistency" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E25 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E25 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Materials and methods, Data selection and preparation" ; stm:quote "For each of 23 reviews in Issue 8 (2023), the original search strategy was replicated using identical keyword combinations on the databases specified in the reviews’ appendices" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E26 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E26 ; stm:status "absent" ; stm:location "not found" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E27 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E27 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Materials and methods, LLM pipelines for automated abstract screening" ; stm:quote "GPT-3.5 Turbo (gpt-3.5-turbo-0125), GPT-4 Turbo (gpt-4-0125-preview), and GPT-4o (gpt-4o-2024-05-13) models were accessed through the Azure OpenAI Service, using the OpenAI (1.23.2) Python package" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E28 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E28 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Materials and methods, Data selection and preparation" ; stm:quote "A comprehensive dataset of all 119 695 articles, which was used for final evaluation of optimal LLM-prompt combinations, as a faithful reflection of the real-world task of abstract screening" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E29 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E29 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Results, LLM can match or exceed human screening performance on a balanced dataset" ; stm:quote "These results indicated that review-centric factors—such as clarity and comprehensiveness of reporting—may affect abstract screening performance in addition to LLM and human factors such as intrinsic aptitude, expertise, and prompt engineering" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E30 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E30 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Materials and methods, LLM pipelines for automated abstract screening" ; stm:quote "LLM screening was undertaken using pipelines implementing application programming interface (APIs) for open- and closed-source LLMs" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E31 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E31 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Discussion, limitations" ; stm:quote "Three limitations may have affected the study’s results and conclusions. First, representativeness was limited although a full issue of the Cochrane Database of Systematic Reviews was used to test across a broad range of medical topics" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E32 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E32 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Abstract, Results; and Results, LLMs maintain high sensitivity when extended to a real-world dataset" ; stm:quote "When evaluated on the comprehensive dataset, the best performing LLM-prompt combinations exhibited consistent sensitivity (range 0.756-1.000) but diminished precision (range 0.004-0.096) due to class imbalance" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E33 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E33 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Materials and methods, Evaluation methodology" ; stm:quote "Prompt selection for full dataset evaluation was based on balanced accuracy—the arithmetic mean of sensitivity and specificity. An exception was made for GPT-3.5, where the “heavy” bias prompt was selected despite not exhibiting optimal balanced accuracy" .
stmd:evidence-40119675-E34 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E34 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Results, Prompt design determines LLM screening behavior" ; stm:quote "as recall increased, precision tended to decrease (Pearson’s correlation coefficient, R = −0.47, 95% confidence interval −0.53 to −0.42, P < .001" .
