stmd:evidence-42286747-E01 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E01 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Results, Table 2 column headings" ; stm:quote "Proportion with full agreement Precision Recall/Sensitivity Specificity F1 Accuracy Krippendorff’s alpha" .
stmd:evidence-42286747-E02 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E02 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Results, A proposed workflow, Step 6, and Tables 1 to 3" ; stm:quote "In our case example, we started with 2514 records in total. Of these, 471 records were classified via human consensus in Steps 2 and 2b, while 1647 records received full agreement classification in Step 5." .
stmd:evidence-42286747-E03 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E03 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Results, Table 3, and Table 4" ; stm:quote "Consensus-based screening decision: include Consensus-based screening decision: exclude Full agreement classification: include 49 4 Full agreement classification: exclude 1 348" .
stmd:evidence-42286747-E04 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E04 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Results, Step 6" ; stm:quote "Using this workflow, the total manual workload was reduced by over 70%: in a traditional approach, each of the 2514 records would have required classification by two human reviewers, resulting in 5028 manual classifications." .
stmd:evidence-42286747-E05 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E05 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Abstract, Conclusions, and A proposed workflow" ; stm:quote "A full agreement approach across three LLMs may offer a promising and conservative strategy for title-and-abstract screening in systematic reviews by automating concordant decisions while reserving human review for discordant cases." .
stmd:evidence-42286747-E06 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E06 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Results, Step 6: resolving the remaining cases without full agreement" ; stm:quote "If the human reviewer disagrees with the LLM majority-classification, a second human reviewer is consulted to reach a final consensus." .
stmd:evidence-42286747-E07 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E07 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Introduction" ; stm:quote "these requirements—although methodologically sound—can pose significant barriers for smaller research groups, research groups from low- and middle-income countries, or research groups in underfunded research areas from conducting systematic reviews" .
stmd:evidence-42286747-E08a a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E08a ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Abstract, Methods" ; stm:quote "This approach was examined across six datasets to assess its effectiveness." .
stmd:evidence-42286747-E08b a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E08b ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Results, Table 2" ; stm:quote "Reanalysis of Li et al., 2024 [ 48 ] GPT 3.5; GPT 4.0; Llama Meijboom 2021 0.57 (75 of 132 titles and abstracts) 0,64 1,00 0,72 0,78 0,81 0,62" .
stmd:evidence-42286747-E08c a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E08c ; stm:status "absent" ; stm:location "not found" .
stmd:evidence-42286747-E09 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E09 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Results, Step 4" ; stm:quote "If the key performance metrics for records with full agreement are too low (e.g., Krippendorff’s alpha < 0.8, F1-score < 0.9), the LLMs do not classify the calibration sample with sufficient consistency, making the approach unsuitable for the given review context." .
stmd:evidence-42286747-E10 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E10 ; stm:status "absent" ; stm:location "not found" .
stmd:evidence-42286747-E11 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E11 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Introduction, LLMs in systematic reviews" ; stm:quote "because they generate plausible outputs from learned statistical patterns rather than applying explicit methodological rules, they may hallucinate, fabricate, or over-infer information, omit relevant studies or details, and misrepresent or oversimplify source content" .
stmd:evidence-42286747-E12 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E12 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Results, Step 6, and Discussion" ; stm:quote "To resolve these cases, the methodologist (Reviewer 2) created a new file containing only the 396 remaining records, including the title and abstract text but excluding LLM classifications." .
stmd:evidence-42286747-E13 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E13 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Discussion and conclusion" ; stm:quote "The approach is therefore best understood not as a replacement for reviewer judgment, but as a conservative model for selectively automating those screening decisions for which full agreement across models is achieved." .
stmd:evidence-42286747-E14 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E14 ; stm:status "partial" ; stm:location "Results, Step 3, and Data availability" ; stm:quote "To ensure replicability, we outline one possible step-by-step implementation using Google Sheets." .
stmd:evidence-42286747-E15 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E15 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Results, Step 4" ; stm:quote "Ideally, these LLMs should come from different model families, as LLMs from distinct architectures often produce different classification decisions, even when provided with the same input (see [ 48 , 59 ])." .
stmd:evidence-42286747-E16 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E16 ; stm:status "present" ; stm:location "Results, Step 2 and Step 2b" ; stm:quote "Two hundred forty-nine of all 2514 records were independently reviewed by three reviewers: an expert in the field, a methodologist without subject-matter expertise, and a research assistant." .
stmd:evidence-42286747-E17 a stm:EvidenceItem ; stm:field stmd:field-E17 ; stm:status "absent" ; stm:location "not found" .
